  "extraction_notes": "Report is titled 'Annual Water Quality Report 2025' / '2025 Consumer Confidence Report' and all routine sample dates are 2025, but the About-This-Report sentence says 'January 1 - December 31, 2024' (apparent carry-over typo); data_year recorded as 2025. Lead/copper AL, MCLG and unit labels appear inconsistent in the table (AL 0.015 with ppb header; MCLG 2 for lead, 0.17 for copper) and the fluoride MCL/PHG appear swapped; all copied as printed. Ranges printed high-to-low ('9-8', '5-4') were stored as low/high. Tables for lead/copper and sodium/hardness are on PDF page 5, primary standards page 6, secondary standards and raw-source coliform page 7, surface water treatment page 8. The report states no violations ('our system had no violations'). In this report the 'Level Detected' column equals the range high in most rows (e.g. hardness 157 with range 138-157, TDS 208 with range 168-208), i.e. it is the highest result rather than an average, so value_basis is recorded as 'level detected' and average is left null except for chlorine (monthly sampling)."
